{"code":"51-6031.00","title":"Sewing Machine Operators","description":"Operate or tend sewing machines to join, reinforce, decorate, or perform related sewing operations in the manufacture of garment or nongarment products.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":6.78,"share":0.5678},"I":{"score":1.37,"share":0.0363},"A":{"score":1.75,"share":0.0737},"S":{"score":1.16,"share":0.0157},"E":{"score":1.15,"share":0.0147},"C":{"score":3.97,"share":0.2917}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":12149,"text":"Monitor machine operation to detect problems such as defective stitching, breaks in thread, or machine malfunctions.","core":true,"importance":4.39,"relevance":94.1,"frequency":5.91},{"id":12165,"text":"Cut materials according to specifications, using blades, scissors, or electric knives.","core":false,"importance":4.37,"relevance":57.93,"frequency":5.72},{"id":12151,"text":"Place spools of thread, cord, or other materials on spindles, insert bobbins, and thread ends through machine guides and components.","core":true,"importance":4.32,"relevance":95.63,"frequency":5.93},{"id":12150,"text":"Position items under needles, using marks on machines, clamps, templates, or cloth as guides.","core":true,"importance":4.31,"relevance":82.17,"frequency":5.98},{"id":12153,"text":"Guide garments or garment parts under machine needles and presser feet to sew parts together.","core":true,"importance":4.26,"relevance":87.51,"frequency":6.17},{"id":12152,"text":"Match cloth pieces in correct sequences prior to sewing them, and verify that dye lots and patterns match.","core":true,"importance":4.17,"relevance":72.79,"frequency":5.54},{"id":12166,"text":"Remove holding devices and finished items from machines.","core":true,"importance":4.17,"relevance":75.91,"frequency":6.04},{"id":12160,"text":"Fold or stretch edges or lengths of items while sewing to facilitate forming specified sections.","core":true,"importance":4.16,"relevance":88.32,"frequency":5.52},{"id":12159,"text":"Cut excess material or thread from finished products.","core":true,"importance":4.15,"relevance":79.96,"frequency":5.92},{"id":12157,"text":"Select supplies such as fasteners and thread, according to job requirements.","core":true,"importance":4.14,"relevance":88.78,"frequency":5.25},{"id":12162,"text":"Examine and measure finished articles to verify conformance to standards, using rulers.","core":true,"importance":4.12,"relevance":74.37,"frequency":5.38},{"id":12154,"text":"Start and operate or tend machines, such as single or double needle serging and flat-bed felling machines, to automatically join, reinforce, or decorate material or articles.","core":true,"importance":4.09,"relevance":72.75,"frequency":5.41},{"id":12156,"text":"Inspect garments, and examine repair tags and markings on garments to locate defects or damage, and mark errors as necessary.","core":false,"importance":4.08,"relevance":55.4,"frequency":5.11},{"id":12155,"text":"Record quantities of materials processed.","core":true,"importance":4.04,"relevance":71.31,"frequency":5.39},{"id":12163,"text":"Turn knobs, screws, and dials to adjust settings of machines, according to garment styles and equipment performance.","core":true,"importance":4.02,"relevance":83.45,"frequency":5.14},{"id":12171,"text":"Attach buttons, hooks, zippers, fasteners, or other accessories to fabric, using feeding hoppers or clamp holders.","core":false,"importance":4.02,"relevance":54.62,"frequency":5.42},{"id":12164,"text":"Repair or alter items by adding replacement parts or missing stitches.","core":true,"importance":3.96,"relevance":79.67,"frequency":5},{"id":12169,"text":"Attach tape, trim, appliques, or elastic to specified garments or garment parts, according to item specifications.","core":true,"importance":3.96,"relevance":73.41,"frequency":4.77},{"id":12168,"text":"Position material or articles in clamps, templates, or hoop frames prior to automatic operation of machines.","core":false,"importance":3.94,"relevance":38.87,"frequen